; exclude_index_out_of_range: EXCLUDE writes a coefficient and must bound it.
;
; ISA.md placed no bound on these indices, so neither VM contradicted it and
; the divergence was unpinnable until the spec said which behaviour was
; right. It now says IndexOutOfBounds, for consistency with every other
; model-writing opcode, and this vector is what holds both VMs to it.
;
; The failure this removes is the expensive one: the Rust VM inserted
; quad(2, 100) on a model whose variables are 0..4, so the mutual-exclusion
; constraint the program asked for was attached to a variable that does not
; exist. It constrained nothing, the model solved cleanly, and nothing in the
; output distinguished it from a correct run.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 2           ; i, in range
PUSH 100         ; j, far past the extent
PUSH 1           ; penalty
EXCLUDE r0
HALT
